    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA 17:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "When David had come to Mahanaim, Shobi the son of Nahash of Rabbah of the children of Ammon, and Machir the son of Ammiel of Lodebar, and Barzillai the Gileadite of Rogelim,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 19:31",
        "textualBasisJa": "Barzillai the Gileadite came down from Rogelim; and he went over the Jordan with the king to conduct him over the Jordan."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 19:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Barzillai was a very aged man, even eighty years old. He had provided the king with sustenance while he stayed at Mahanaim, for he was a very great man."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 19:33",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king said to Barzillai, “Come over with me, and I will sustain you with me in Jerusalem.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 19:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "Barzillai said to the king, “How many are the days of the years of my life, that I should go up with the king to Jerusalem?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA 19:39",
        "textualBasisJa": "All the people went over the Jordan, and the king went over. Then the king kissed Barzillai and blessed him; and he returned to his own place."
      }
    ],
